# .why no OnCalendar: the payload does the clock math, in a PINNED timezone.
#   an OnCalendar here would read the BOX's timezone, so a grove on UTC and a
#   laptop on local would enforce two different windows from one declaration.
#
# .why OnUnitActiveSec and not two triggers at 08:00 / 20:00: a box asleep at
#   08:00 misses a trigger and sits allowed all day. a periodic converge
#   self-heals, and costs at most one interval of drift.
#
# ⚠️ .the CADENCE is 2/hr, so a boundary can be up to 30 minutes late
#   that is the declared trade: the gate is a courtesy fence around a human's
#   hours, not a security control, and a re-ask every 5 minutes bought 6x the
#   wakeups to sharpen an edge nobody measures.
#   ⇒ a box that must close ON the minute needs a different mechanism, never a
#     smaller interval here — the drift is bounded by design, not by accident.
#
# .why 1min after boot: a box woken inside the window must close the gate
#   promptly, not up to half an hour later.

[Unit]
Description=Re-ask the open-hours policy twice an hour

[Timer]
OnBootSec=1min
OnUnitActiveSec=30min

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
